# Lightweight Renewable Energy ETL Pipeline (Polars + DuckDB)

An energy-efficient Data Engineering pipeline built on Linux Mint that ingests real-time solar radiation and wind speed metrics from the **Open-Meteo API**, processes them in-memory using **Polars**, and stores analytical aggregations in **DuckDB**.

## Why This Stack? (Green Software Approach)
Designed to run smoothly on low-resource hardware (**4 GB RAM**), minimizing CPU cycles and memory footprint compared to heavy JVM-based or containerized stacks:
* **Package Management:** `uv` (fast dependency resolution in Rust)
* **Data Processing:** Polars + Apache Arrow (zero-copy columnar transformations)
* **Analytical Storage:** DuckDB (embedded OLAP database)

## Data Architecture
`Open-Meteo REST API (JSON)` ➔ `Polars DataFrame (Transform & Feature Engineering)` ➔ `DuckDB (SQL Warehouse)`

## Quickstart Guide

1. Clone the repository:
   ```bash
   git clone https://github.com
   cd YOUR_REPO_NAME
   ```

2. Install dependencies via `uv`:
   ```bash
   uv sync
   ```

3. Run the ETL pipeline:
   ```bash
   uv run renewable_pipeline.py
   ```
EOF

